<title>THAILAND: Thailand removes cross-border rice trade limits.</title>
<headline>Thailand removes cross-border rice trade limits.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Thai government has removed limits imposed on cross-border rice trade in a move to boost rice exports, a commerce ministry source said on Thursday.</p>
<p>In the past, the amount of rice sold across the border to neighbouring countries such as Laos, Malaysia and Burma was limited to 500,000 baht ($20,000) per day for each exporter, the source told Reuters.</p>
<p>Thailand aims to export at least five million tonnes of rice for 1997.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
</text>
